+# Zombie Survival
+
+**Games & Worlds → ☣️ Zombie Survival** in the left menu opens `/zombie-survival`:
+a third-person survival game set in a small town after the outbreak, in the
+spirit of DayZ, Vein and Project Zomboid. You scavenge every building,
+barricade doors and windows, treat wounds, run generators, and break into the
+town's computers (the police terminal, CCTV and keypads all work). It is
+played with a keyboard and mouse.
+
+It is a separate project — the `zombie-survival-game/` folder of
+[`93jessycollin93-del/eru`](https://github.com/93jessycollin93-del/eru), branch
+`claude/zombie-survival-game-repo-v1v6hp` — and ships here as a finished build,
+the same way [the PC](PC_EMBED.md) does. Nothing in it talks to Supabase or any
+account: runs are saved in this browser's IndexedDB, on this device only.
+
+## How it works
+
+- `public/zombie-survival/` holds the game's production build, made with
+  `--base ./` so every file it loads is relative to that folder. An absolute
+  `/assets/…` would fetch Jackie's own bundles instead.
+- `src/pages/ZombieSurvival.tsx` frames `/zombie-survival/index.html` under a
+  slim header: back to Jackie, full screen, restart, and open in its own tab.
+- **Saving on the way out.** Leaving the page destroys the frame, and a save the
+  game starts while it is being torn down may never commit. So Back and
+  Restart first post `{type: "zombie-survival:save", id}` to the frame; the
+  game (its `src/game/embedBridge.ts`) runs its autosave and answers
+  `{type: "zombie-survival:saved", id, saved, reason}`. The game keeps its own
+  autosave rules — it won't save while something is hunting you or mid-climb —
+  and when it says no, or doesn't answer within 2.5 s, the page says why and
+  asks before leaving. Both sides check that the message comes from the other
+  frame on the same origin.
+- **Open in its own tab** opens the game at once and has this copy save and
+  step aside, so two copies never take turns overwriting one autosave.
+- **A build that wasn't deployed** doesn't 404: the host answers
+  `/zombie-survival/index.html` with Jackie's own `index.html`. The page checks
+  the frame's title after it loads and shows "The game isn't in this build"
+  instead of booting Jackie inside her own frame.
+- Jackie's service worker leaves the game out of its precache (every visitor
+  would download it whether they play or not) and out of the SPA navigation
+  fallback (which would answer the frame with Jackie's shell). Runtime caching
+  picks the files up the first time the game is played, so it then works
+  offline.
+- `src/test/zombie-survival.test.tsx` pins all of the above: the menu entry, the
+  route, the shipped build and its relative paths, the save handshake, and the
+  service-worker rules.
+
+## Refreshing the build
+
+After the game changes, rebuild it straight into this repo:
+
+```sh
+# in eru/zombie-survival-game
+npm install
+npm run build:embed -- ../../sasjacky777-d1033916/public/zombie-survival
+```
+
+(`build:embed` is `vite build --base ./ --emptyOutDir --outDir`; point it at
+wherever this repo is checked out.) Then run
+`npx vitest run src/test/zombie-survival.test.tsx` here and commit the refreshed
+`public/zombie-survival/`.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- No touch controls yet. On a phone or tablet the page opens the game and says
+  so plainly.
+- Saves stay on the device and browser they were made in; there is no cloud
+  save.
+- Every game update can change the town. A save made before such an update is
+  refused with a message rather than loaded into the wrong town.
